@@ -161,6 +161,7 @@ A second sprint of validations testing per-cancer architectural disruption signa
 | **VAL-094** | **EpiSCORE BreastRef sub-cell-type Stage 2 resolution test on GSE51057 + GSE51032, all 4 TTD windows** | n=329 GSE51057 + n=845 GSE51032 (full cohort, all TTD windows). Pre-registered (SHA `501fafad68fa9363…`) sealed 2026-04-26 before β-access. EpiSCORE BreastRef mref (468 markers Entrez-ID × 7 cell types after dropping 'weight' meta-column: Basal, Endothelial, Adipocyte, Fibroblast, Luminal, tissue-Lymphocyte, tissue-Macrophage) bridged to 450K CpGs via probeInfo450k (19,357 unique Entrez IDs in bridge); top-80 specificity Entrez markers per cell type → 1,162-1,422 unique CpGs each; A-score against secretory H_min 0.8433 · **Outcome `O2_DISTRIBUTED_AS_LOYFER`**: all 7 EpiSCORE BreastRef cell types produce nearly identical per-window d values across all 4 TTD windows in both cohorts (within 0.10-0.16 of each other). At >10yr GSE51057 EpiSCORE produces d=+1.01 to +1.17 across all 7 cell types; this does not replicate to GSE51032 (d=+0.20 to +0.33). At 0-2yr GSE51032 EpiSCORE mean d=+0.48 matches Loyfer breast tile +0.49. **Resolution-collapse pattern**: 7 sub-cell types behave as one coherent signal because discriminating CpGs cluster in correlated genomic regions across sub-cell types. EpiSCORE BreastRef is therefore NOT added to breast-epic v2.3 as a per-sub-cell-type discriminator. Cookbook-wide implication: EpiSCORE-style gene-indexed sub-tissue references should be tested for resolution-collapse before being added to any card's per-sub-cell-type Stage 2 layer. CHK-3.1 PASS, CHK-3.2 PASS · breast-LL-007 added | [GSE51057](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSE51057) + [GSE51032](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSE51032) + [Zhu Teschendorff 2022 EpiSCORE](https://github.com/aet21/EpiSCORE) reference matrices |
 | **VAL-095** | **UniLIFE 19-cell vs Salas 450K 6-cell head-to-head Stage 3 deconvolution on GSE51057 + GSE51032, all 4 TTD windows** | Same cohorts. Pre-registered (SHA `5f74259d5341268e…`) sealed 2026-04-26 before β-access. RPC-style NNLS deconvolution (sum-to-1 normalized, NaN-aware) on UniLIFE Guo 2025 (1,906 CpGs × 19 immune cell types: 7 pan-lifespan + 12 adult-specific subtypes) head-to-head with Salas 450K legacy IDOL (350 CpGs × 6 cell types). Both atlases 100% CpG coverage in both cohorts via streaming union-CpG extraction (`extract_union_cpgs.py`, 26,453 target CpGs from 26,453 union, 98.9% extraction yield) · **Outcome `O1_RESOLUTION_GAIN`**: two replicating findings with bootstrap 95% CIs that exclude zero in both cohorts: **aTreg (regulatory T) at >10yr**: GSE51057 d=+1.26 [+0.39, +2.26] (n_cases=11, n_ctrl=177), GSE51032 d=+0.79 [+0.33, +1.33] (n_cases=36, n_ctrl=424) — Salas CD4T pooled at same window: +0.36 / +0.03 · **aBnv (naive B-cell) at 0-2yr**: GSE51057 d=+0.44 [+0.15, +0.76], GSE51032 d=+0.49 [+0.23, +0.77] — Salas Bcell pooled at same window: +0.31 / +0.36 · UniLIFE separates regulatory T-cell signal from the larger CD4T pool, and naive B-cell signal from the pooled B-cell compartment. Pan-lifespan UniLIFE markers mostly mirror Salas 6-cell signal — resolution gain sits in the 12 adult-specific subtypes. Healthy aTreg baseline is small (mean ≈ 0.006 in controls of both cohorts); d magnitude reflects relative shift on small absolute baseline · **Production decision**: Salas Blood.EPIC IDOL (or Salas 450K legacy on legacy cohorts) remains production Stage 3 baseline. UniLIFE added as parallel adult-specific subtype overlay per Heath sign-off 2026-04-26 ("EDEAR RUN-EVERYTHING — every IDAT runs Stage 1+2+3 with ALL panels/atlases regardless of any stage result"). Reports cite both layers when UniLIFE adult-specific subtypes show signal exceeding their replication thresholds. Test 2 framework-level claims blocked on OQ-2026-01 immune-atlas staging per CCL-030; lymphoid-vs-myeloid pattern documented in VAL-095 outcome.md is observation-only · breast-LL-006 added | [GSE51057](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSE51057) + [GSE51032](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSE51032) + [UniLIFE Guo 2025](https://doi.org/10.1186/s13073-025-01493-x) (Genome Med 17:63) + [Salas 2018 Blood.450K legacy](https://github.com/immunomethylomics/FlowSorted.Blood.EPIC) |
 | **VAL-096** | **TTD-window stratification on Loyfer 25-tile per-tile A-scores (re-analysis of VAL-093 per-sample CSV)** | Same cohorts, all four TTD windows (0-2yr, 2-5yr, 5-10yr, >10yr). Pre-registered (SHA `01247146d955ad28…`) sealed 2026-04-26 before re-analysis. Pure re-slicing of VAL-093's per-sample A-score CSV by TTD window with bootstrap 95% CIs (1000 iterations, BCa-equivalent). RNG seed 20260426 · **Outcome `O1_BREAST_TILE_FIRES_NEAR_DIAGNOSIS` (partial)** + **`O4_PATTERN_AMPLIFIES_AT_NEAR_DX`** (steady-state distributed pattern documented). Two-component temporal model: (1) **Persistent distributed cellular-aging-drift** across pancreatic + cycling-class tiles at all four pre-dx windows in both cohorts — pancreatic beta cells GSE51057 d=+1.02 (>10yr) → +0.40 (0-2yr), pancreatic acinar +0.91 → +0.52, pancreatic duct +0.99 → +0.04, kidney +0.73 → +0.54, head/neck-larynx +0.75 → +0.11, colon epithelial +0.72 → +0.29; (2) **Late-localizing breast tile** rises from d=+0.20/+0.10 (>10yr) → +0.05/+0.19 (5-10yr) → +0.14/+0.16 (2-5yr) → **+0.43/+0.49 (0-2yr)** in both cohorts, both directionally exceeding 0.5 threshold approach; (3) **Immune-tile inversion-near-diagnosis** — three immune-class tiles attenuate or sign-flip at 0-2yr: monocytes +0.33 → −0.35 GSE51057 / +0.00 → −0.40 GSE51032; neutrophils drift toward negative; erythrocyte progenitors +0.83 → −0.14 GSE51057 large attenuation. CCL-035 candidate flagged for further investigation. The two components are additive at 0-2yr — both the breast tile and several persistently-elevated tiles still show concurrent elevation. **Stage 2 reports for samples at long pre-dx now describe the distributed pattern explicitly** rather than asserting breast localization; the localization step happens near clinical diagnosis. VAL-060 (paired d=+0.676 tumor vs adjacent-normal) and VAL-096 0-2yr breast tile (d=+0.43/+0.49) are the cleanest pieces of breast-localized Stage 2 evidence. CHK-3.2 PASS (0/25 tiles cross 1-anchor-SD threshold). Heatmap deliverable `VAL-096_window_tile_heatmap.png` · breast-LL-005 added | [GSE51057](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSE51057) + [GSE51032](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSE51032) + [nloyfer/meth_atlas](https://github.com/nloyfer/meth_atlas) reference atlas |
+| **VAL-097** | **Never-smoker LUAD tissue 25-tile per-class A-score on GSE256092 with cross-cohort baseline against TCGA-LUAD adjacent-normal** | n=141 GSE256092 Korean NSLA tumor tissue (EPIC, SWAN normalized) vs n=29 TCGA-LUAD adjacent-normal lung tissue (HM450, sesame level3, downloaded fresh from GDC public API per VAL-063 LUAD_matched_manifest.json). Pre-registered (SHA `9a1bd45e240eea7a…`) sealed 2026-04-28 before β-access. Run-everything Loyfer 25-tile per-class A-score, bootstrap 10000 d CI, top-100 marker CpGs per tile, RNG seed 20260428, runtime 81s · **Outcome `O5_BASELINE_DOMINATED`** (assigned by honest reading per CHK-4.8; auto-assigned O2_CYCLING_DISTRIBUTED criterion was structurally degenerate when baseline_anchor_SD and case_vs_reference_d are computed identically). Lung_cells tile d = −0.27 [−0.54, +0.02] — the lung tile is the SECOND-WEAKEST in the entire 25-tile panel; 22 of 25 tiles uniformly positive; 11 of 25 tiles breach >3 anchor-SD on CHK-3.2; top-1 ΔA call is B-cells_EPIC in 79/141 (56%) of patients. The result is dominated by three stacked sources of non-biological variance: SWAN-vs-sesame preprocessing pipeline mismatch + Korean-vs-Western population baseline shift + bulk-tumor-vs-adjacent-normal cell-composition difference. Cross-cohort comparison without explicit batch correction (ComBat / BMIQ / RUV) is structurally invalid for this cohort pair · **LL-CROSS-COHORT-CALIBRATION** logged: when two cohorts use different preprocessing pipelines AND different platforms AND different populations without batch correction, β-value scale shift dominates disease signal. **EDEAR commercial deployment is unaffected** — single-pipeline patient-vs-internal-reference comparisons have no cross-cohort calibration problem. **LL-PRELOCK-DEGENERATE-COMPARATOR** logged: future O5 criteria must test breach pattern directly (≥3 tiles >3 anchor-SD AND ≥80% same-direction = baseline-dominated). Within-cohort GSE256092 stratification (sex × age decade × stage) IS interpretable on its own terms and is reported in `stratified.json`. Never-smoker LUAD tissue tile pattern remains uncharacterized; recommended follow-up VAL-098 on GSE235414 (driver-stratified LUAD with internal matched adjacent-normal samples in same cohort, same pipeline) · CHK-2.7 PASS, CHK-3.2 BREACHED-AS-EXPECTED-AT-MAGNITUDE-EXCEEDING-PRELOCK, CHK-4.8 honest revision applied, CHK-7.6 reproducibility triple complete | [GSE256092](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSE256092) + [TCGA-LUAD adjacent-normal via NIH GDC](https://api.gdc.cancer.gov/data/) + [nloyfer/meth_atlas](https://github.com/nloyfer/meth_atlas) reference atlas |
 
 **Sprint summary.** Seven tissue and plasma validations (VAL-058 through VAL-064) all PASS at the prereg-sealed Cohen's d ≥ 0.5 threshold, plus one exploratory urine-arm specimen comparison (VAL-065), plus the pancreatic-epic v0.1 build (VAL-066/067/068/069) which delivered three independent tissue cohorts plus a directional Xu-538 fallback panel. Two framework-relevant stratification findings emerged: (1) **smoking stratification is mandatory for lung-epic** — TCGA-LUAD is 76% ever-smoker and the never-smoker arm (n=2) is underpowered for independent inference. (2) **Chronic viral hepatitis blunts the paired tumor-vs-adjacent-normal contrast in HCC** through methylation drift in the adjacent-normal liver tissue ("field defect" per Villanueva 2015), shrinking the paired contrast even though the tumor architecture is genuinely disrupted. Non-viral HCC (alcohol/NAFLD) shows classical secretory-class magnitude (d ≈ +0.66, comparable to breast secretory). The pattern parallels the lung smoking finding and may generalize: chronic disease-driver exposures drive adjacent-normal field defects that need to be controlled for in paired-tissue analyses. **VAL-065 is exploratory:** GSE119260 (Brikun 2018) is the only public EPIC 850K urine methylation prostate cohort and contains only n=4 advanced-disease patients (all bone metastatic, Gleason 4+4 to 5+5). Sample size precludes substrate-vs-substrate inference. The observed urine vs benign tissue paired d = −2.39 (urine A-score dramatically lower than benign tissue in all 4 patients) was anticipated by the pre-registration as O5_UNEXPECTED and is documented as an open question pending a larger urine methylation prostate cohort with healthy controls and mixed disease stages.
 
